    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Newly unified <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>'s late bid for colonies, spanning <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrea">Eritrea</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-somaliland">Somaliland</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dodecanese">Dodecanese</a> and, briefly, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>.</li><li>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Mussolini</a> it became a vehicle for Fascist dreams of a new Roman empire, enforced with poison gas, camps and racial laws.</li><li>It collapsed within three years in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>, and the 1947 Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> formally stripped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> of its colonies.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>In 1938 Governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italo-balbo">Italo Balbo</a> oversaw the arrival in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a> of some twenty thousand Italian settlers in a single state-organised convoy.</p></aside>
    </section>

